<title>USA: Northwestern University repriced, yield raised.</title>
<headline>Northwestern University repriced, yield raised.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Chicago Capital Markets Inc said Wednesday it repriced $20 million Illinois Educational Facilities Authority bonds, for Northwestern University, raising the yield in 2000 to 4.75 percent from 4.70 percent.</p>
<p>The repricing follows:</p>
<p>ILLINOIS EDUCATIONAL FACILITIES AUTHORITY</p>
<p>RE: $20,000,000*</p>
<p>REVENUE REFUNDING BONDS</p>
<p>NORTHWESTERN UNIVERSITY, SERIES 1996</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD RECEIVED</p>
<p>    MOODY'S: Aa1		   S&amp;P: AA</p>
<p>    DATED: 09/15/1996	  FIRST COUPON: 12/01/1996</p>
<p>DUE: 12/01</p>
<p>ALL BONDS ARE PRICED AT PAR.</p>
<p>MATURITY		 AMOUNT*    COUPON</p>
<p>12/01/2000	     20,000M    4.75  %</p>
<p>CALL FEATURES: NON-CALLABLE</p>
<p>* - APPROXIMATE SUBJECT TO CHANGE</p>
<p>The compliance addendum MSRB Rule G-11 will apply.</p>
<p>The award is expected Wednesday, September 25, 1996.</p>
<p>Delivery is expected on October 1, 1996.</p>
<p>This issue is book entry through DTC.</p>
<p>First Chicago Capital Markets, Inc.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
